  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New **Panel setups** window, opened from the View door's \"Panel setups...\"\n  row. It saves the dock as it stands under a name, loads a saved\n  arrangement back, deletes one, toggles auto-load, and reaches the\n  existing \"Reset layout\".\n- Panel open state, attach side, split sizes, tab order, active tab,\n  collapsed leaves and float rects are kept as the dock's own egui_dock\n  JSON behind a `camcraft-panel-setups/1` format tag.\n- Setups are application settings in `panel-setups.json` beside the\n  theme, never the project file. Auto-load is on by default.\n- A corrupt or older file, or a dock that breaks the permanence law\n  (a floating viewport, a rootless main area), loads the default layout\n  with a diagnostic. A load is view state: it rides a one-frame mailbox,\n  never the command history.\n\n## Needs your decision\n\n- `egui_dock` now has its `serde` feature on, and `camcraft-ui` gains the\n  existing workspace `serde` as a direct dependency. This is a dependency\n  change: it needs the `needs-maintainer` label (agents cannot set it).\n  The rationale is in `docs/decisions/2339-panel-setups.md`: the saved\n  arrangement keeps the dock's own tree, so splits, tab order, collapsed\n  leaves and float rects survive exactly.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `docs/decisions/2339-panel-setups.md` - format choice and dropped\n  alternatives (hand-rolled leaf JSON, egui_dock's own save format).\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/panel_setups.rs`:\n  `save_then_load_restores_the_panel_setup`,\n  `the_saved_setup_starts_the_next_run`,\n  `auto_load_off_starts_with_the_default_layout`,\n  `a_corrupt_setup_loads_the_default_layout_with_a_diagnostic`,\n  `an_older_setups_file_starts_the_default_layout`,\n  `a_viewport_in_a_float_is_refused`.\n- `layout_window_panel_setups` (in `page_layout_windows.rs`).\n- App-side store tests in `crates/app/src/prefs.rs` (lib unit tests).\n\n## Gate\n\n- `camcraft-ui` lib tests: 1224 passed, 0 failed, 7 ignored.\n- `camcraft-app` lib tests: 379 passed, 0 failed, 1 ignored.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A multi-monitor float rect on a second desktop.\n- Setups shared between Windows and Linux runs (same JSON, not tried).\n\nChangelog: The Panel setups window saves and restores the panel arrangement across runs.\n\nFixes #2339\n",
